<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>Astro on Cloudflare</title>
    <style>
      :root { color-scheme: light dark; }
      body {
        font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
        max-width: 540px;
        margin: 3rem auto;
        padding: 0 1rem;
        line-height: 1.6;
      }
      nav { margin-bottom: 2rem; display: flex; gap: 1rem; }
      ul { margin: 1.5rem 0 2rem 1.5rem; }
      li { margin-bottom: 0.75rem; }
      a { color: inherit; }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <nav>
      <strong>Home</strong>
      <a href="/ssg">SSG</a>
      <a href="/ssr">SSR</a>
    </nav>

    <h1>Astro on Cloudflare</h1>
    <p>Simple demonstration comparing static and server rendering:</p>

    <ul>
      <li><a href="/ssg"><strong>SSG Page (/ssg)</strong></a> — Built once at compile time. Values stay frozen across reloads.</li>
      <li><a href="/ssr"><strong>SSR Page (/ssr)</strong></a> — Rendered on-demand by the Worker. Values change on every reload.</li>
    </ul>
  </body>
</html>
